/**
 * ESABCC report (2024, 'Towards EU climate neutrality') progress
 * indicators — primary historical time series for each named
 * indicator (O1-O3, E1-E6, I1-I7, T1-T6, B1-B6, A1-A7, L1-L8, plus
 * the finance/innovation chapter figures 78, 80-86).
 *
 * Generated by scripts/esabcc-indicators/build.py from the report's
 * underlying-data workbook. Numbers are rounded; full precision is
 * preserved in scripts/esabcc-indicators/extract.json. Where the
 * primary publisher (Eurostat / EEA / EAFO / EHPA / IRENA) has a
 * stable API, the indicator id is also registered in the live-source
 * registry so 'Refresh from source' pulls fresh values.
 *
 * Cross-reference with ECNO_INDICATORS via the `duplicateOf` field:
 * the ESABCC indicator is treated as the authoritative copy, and the
 * ECNO entry stays around as an `additional` indicator covering the
 * same concept (kept so projects that already linked to that id
 * don't break).
 *
 * NOTE: two sets of edits are layered on top of the bare generator
 * output and would be lost by a blind full regen:
 *  1. `afterReport: true` points (post-2021 values pulled by the
 *     live-source refresh / migration 055 backfill); and
 *  2. the completeness-pass block near the end of the array (the
 *     report figures that were missing — I2, A2, A4, A5, A6, B3, B4,
 *     L2, I7a/b/c). These are generated by `build.py --new-only` and
 *     appended in place. Regenerate new entries with that flag rather
 *     than rewriting the whole file. See
 *     docs/Indicator-Database-Missing-Indicators-Update.md.
 */
